// Pins millimeter storage for the case most likely to mislead a consumer: a
// file whose default length unit is not millimeters, where the author writes
// bare numbers. Here `distance = 500` means 500 inches, and the view stores
// 12700 millimeters.
//
// Before lengths were canonicalized, this stored the number 500 tagged as a
// file-default length. A consumer that read the number and assumed
// millimeters would have placed the camera 25.4 times too close, and nothing
// in the value would have looked wrong.
@settings(experimentalFeatures = allow, defaultLengthUnit = inch)

view = view::oriented(
  view::Orientation::Front,
  target = [1, 0, 0],
  distance = 500,
)
